{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dp5ZvSd35CsK7YL1q3k3WY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Verify the amica-python → jamica rename: correct, scoped, and nothing broken\n2\t\n3\t**Task (code-review / correctness audit, not a general review).** We renamed Sina's JAX AMICA impl\n4\tfrom *amica-python* to **jamica** in this benchmark repo. It must be **display-only and scoped to the\n5\tchunk-size study** — reports + that study's tidy data — and must **not** touch the shared harness, the\n6\traw/committed result data, or accidentally rename look-alikes. Your job: confirm it is correct and\n7\tbroke nothing, citing the actual files at HEAD. State your model + version first.\n8\t\n9\t## Background (the saga you are auditing the NET result of)\n10\t1. `0cd9e05` — a mistaken **repo-wide** rename (harness keys, committed measures, everything). Reverted.\n11\t2. `0d7a23e` — `git revert` of `0cd9e05` (should have fully restored the pre-rename state).\n12\t3. `6fb4b63` (**HEAD**) — the intended **scoped, display-only** rename.\n13\t\n14\tSo the **net effect** of the whole saga is `git diff 9dbf9b5..HEAD` (9dbf9b5 = the commit *before* the\n15\trename campaign). It should be **only** the 7 files under `benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/`.\n16\t\n17\t## What \"correct\" means here\n18\t- **Display = jamica**: the report/showcase *generators* (`gen_report.py`, `gen_showcase.py`), their\n19\t  rendered HTML, and the study's tidy `chunk_sweep_data.csv` show `jamica`.\n20\t- **Machinery + raw data = unchanged** (`amica_python_jax*`): the orchestrator\n21\t  `benchmark/comparator/implementation_perf.py`, the runner `benchmark/comparator/runners/run_amica_python.py`,\n22\t  all committed result JSONs / legacy measures, and the vendored `amica_python/` package — these keep the\n23\t  original run-time keys **on purpose**.\n24\t\n25\t## Verification checklist (please actually run these against the HEAD tree)\n26\t1. **Scope.** Is the net change (vs `9dbf9b5`) confined to `results/xperf_chunksize/`? Grep the tree:\n27\t   the harness (`implementation_perf.py`, `run_amica_python.py`) must still contain `amica_python_jax`\n28\t   and must contain **no** `jamica`. Confirm `run_amica_python.py` still exists (was NOT renamed to\n29\t   `run_jamica.py` — that was part of the reverted commit).\n30\t2. **No look-alike corruption.** Grep the whole repo for accidental damage: `scott` is *also* an\n31\t   \"amica-python\" package — it must stay `scott-huberty` / `scott_huberty_torch`. Also confirm intact:\n32\t   `pyamica`, `pamica` / `pAMICA`, Fortran `amica17` / `fortran_amica17`, the vendored `amica_python/`\n33\t   dir, and paths like `amica-benchmark`. Look for corruption patterns (`pyjamica`, `jamica17`,\n34\t   `scott…jamica`, `jamica-benchmark`) — there should be none.\n35\t3. **Revert was clean.** Does HEAD match the pre-rename state for everything *except* the scoped study\n36\t   files? i.e., did `0d7a23e` fully undo `0cd9e05` with no residue in the harness / committed measures /\n37\t   vendored package?\n38\t4. **Internal consistency of the display rename.** In `gen_report.py` / `gen_showcase.py`, the JAX\n39\t   impl's short dict key was `\"amica\"` and is now `\"jamica\"` — verify it's consistent across **all**\n40\t   dicts/lists that key on it (`IMPLS`, `LABEL`, `KNOB`, `COLOR`, `COMMIT`, `GPU`, `GPU_BAND`, `CPU_RSS`,\n41\t   `CPU_FIT`, `CPU_FIT_MED`, `REAL_OPT`, `CPU_IMPLS`), with no leftover `\"amica\"` key that would raise a\n42\t   KeyError. The generators must still parse/run and emit valid HTML.\n43\t5. **CSV.** `chunk_sweep_data.csv` shows a 208-line diff; we believe that is line-ending normalization\n44\t   plus the `amica`→`jamica` impl-column rename, with the data otherwise identical. Please confirm it is\n45\t   **not** a data change/corruption, and that no `pyamica`/`pamica` row was mangled. (Separately, note if\n46\t   the CSV looks stale vs the real-data report — that's pre-existing, not caused by the rename.)\n47\t6. **Naming claims.** The README naming note states: amica-python → amica → **jamica**\n48\t   (`snesmaeili/jamica`, PyPI `jamica`, import `jamica`); harness keys deliberately unchanged. Is that\n49\t   accurate and are the caveats (scott's separate package, Fortran amica17, cluster paths, ephemeral raw\n50\t   JSONs) correct?\n51\t7. **Bottom line.** Is the rename correct and safe to keep, or is there a real defect? Give a prioritized\n52\t   verdict.\n53\t\n54\t## Net stat (git diff 9dbf9b5..HEAD)\n55\t```\n56\t.../comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/README.md   |  10 +\n57\t .../results/xperf_chunksize/chunk_sweep_data.csv   | 208 ++++++++++-----------\n58\t .../results/xperf_chunksize/gen_report.py          |  64 +++----\n59\t .../results/xperf_chunksize/gen_showcase.py        |  22 +--\n60\t .../xperf_chunksize/realchunk_gpu_showcase.html    |  10 +-\n61\t .../xperf_chunksize/xperf_chunk_report.html        |  40 ++--\n62\t .../xperf_chunk_report_standalone.html             |  40 ++--\n63\t 7 files changed, 202 insertions(+), 192 deletions(-)\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\t## Source diff (the generators + README — the meaningful source changes)\n67\t```diff\n68\tdiff --git a/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/README.md b/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/README.md\n69\tindex 3eda6fb..66e5b9a 100644\n70\t--- a/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/README.md\n71\t+++ b/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/README.md\n72\t@@ -83,3 +83,13 @@ Run through the orchestrator (`implementation_perf.py`) with each impl's best ch\n73\t (`AMICA_CHUNK_SIZE`, `AMICA_PAMICA_BLOCK_SIZE`, `AMICA_PYAMICA_CHUNK`, `AMICA_SCOTT_BATCH`). The\n74\t env-override for the three competitor runners is upstreamed in `../../runners/` (see git log);\n75\t `run_amica_python.py` already honored `AMICA_CHUNK_SIZE`.\n76\t+\n77\t+## Naming: jamica (formerly amica-python)\n78\t+\n79\t+Sina's JAX AMICA was renamed **amica-python → amica → jamica** (`snesmaeili/jamica`, PyPI `jamica`,\n80\t+import `jamica`). This study's **reports and tidy data (`chunk_sweep_data.csv`) display the current\n81\t+name `jamica`**. The shared benchmark harness (runner impl keys `amica_python_jax*`, the orchestrator,\n82\t+and the committed legacy measures) is intentionally left on its **run-time keys** — renaming those\n83\t+would rewrite historical run-time provenance plus the vendored `amica_python/` package and the\n84\t+paper-reproduction bundle, which is a repo-wide migration best owned upstream. So: reports say\n85\t+`jamica`; the machine keys still reflect exactly what the runs stamped (`amica_python_jax*`).\n86\tdiff --git a/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/gen_report.py b/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/gen_report.py\n87\tindex ada77a1..37edf82 100644\n88\t--- a/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/gen_report.py\n89\t+++ b/benchmark/comparator/results/xperf_chunksize/gen_report.py\n90\t@@ -3,22 +3,22 @@\n91\t \n92\t Thesis: chunk size is the dominant performance variable; every implementation is strongly\n93\t chunk-sensitive; defaults are footguns. On the real ds004505 workload (25-subject median, H100,\n94\t-latest main) amica-python is fastest at every chunk and leanest at full-batch. The synthetic\n95\t+latest main) jamica is fastest at every chunk and leanest at full-batch. The synthetic\n96\t \"flat curve\" that once looked like robustness was a JIT-compile artifact (methodology section).\n97\t CPU absolute timings carry a node-contention caveat (see NOTES_measurement.md); CPU *memory* is clean.\n98\t \"\"\"\n99\t import math, os\n100\t \n101\t FULL = 262144\n102\t-IMPLS = [\"amica\", \"pamica\", \"pyamica\", \"scott\"]\n103\t-LABEL = {\"amica\":\"amica-python (JAX)\",\"pamica\":\"pAMICA (sccn)\",\"pyamica\":\"pyamica\",\"scott\":\"scott-huberty\"}\n104\t-KNOB  = {\"amica\":\"chunk_size\",\"pamica\":\"block_size\",\"pyamica\":\"chunk_t\",\"scott\":\"batch_size\",\"fortran\